# SELinux file contexts for atrium (Fedora). The install script registers
# these via semanage fcontext so they persist across system relabels.
# Also serves as reference for RPM packaging.
#
# The daemon binary is labelled xdm_exec_t so systemd starts it in the xdm_t
# display-manager domain. /var/lib/atrium (the atriumdm home and seat-state
# directory) is labelled xdm_var_lib_t, mirroring GDM's /var/lib/gdm, so
# xdm_t can manage seat-state files.
@daemon_bin@           --    system_u:object_r:xdm_exec_t:s0
/var/lib/atrium(/.*)?        system_u:object_r:xdm_var_lib_t:s0
